# Hypothesis Graph: issue 1613

## H0 Observation

- Mode: induction.
- Reproducer: `/tmp/p08g-scratch/reported.rs`.
- Baseline command: `env -u RUSTC -u RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN PATH=/tmp/rustup-shims:$PATH cargo xtask run /tmp/p08g-scratch/reported.rs`.
- Observed baseline: `error[E0999]: type invariant may not hold (when place is folded)` at `self.slot.set(0)`.
- Trace: default diagnostic does not print the predicate. Checker trace shows `self` unfolded to `Container { slot: &mut Slot[s.slot] }`, a reborrow `_3 = &mut *(*_1).0`, then after the call the environment still has `self: Container { slot: &mut Slot[s.slot] }`; the callee post-state on the reborrow is not reflected in the field before folding.

## Differential Narrowing

- H1 (abduction): the explicit field predicate `slot.len > 0` is too strong or malformed.
  - Perturbation: `/tmp/p08g-scratch/no_field_invariant.rs`, same setter but `#[flux_rs::field(&mut Slot[slot])]`.
  - Baseline result: failed with the same fold error.
  - Trajectory: convergent.
  - Verdict: field predicate is incidental; the bug survives without it.

- H2 (abduction): higher-level `Container` folding is essential.
  - Perturbation: `/tmp/p08g-scratch/direct_arg.rs`, direct `fn update_direct(x: &mut {Slot[@n, @f] | n > 0}) { x.set(0); }`.
  - Baseline result: failed with the same fold error.
  - Trajectory: convergent.
  - Verdict: `Container` is incidental; local mutable-reference call folding is sufficient.

- H3 (abduction): any call through `&mut` fails, even if the post-state is identical.
  - Perturbation: `/tmp/p08g-scratch/noop_setter.rs`, setter ensures `self: Slot[n, f]`.
  - Baseline result: verified.
  - Trajectory: divergent/kill.
  - Verdict: the essential condition is a changed callee post-refinement, not the call shape alone.

- H4 (abduction): the issue is limited to higher-order abstract refinements.
  - Perturbation: `/tmp/p08g-scratch/scalar_grow.rs`, scalar-only abstract sort `len` changes from `n` to `n + 1`.
  - Baseline result: failed with the same fold error.
  - Trajectory: convergent.
  - Verdict: not limited to function-valued refinements; changed abstract refinement state through a mutable reborrow is the general trigger.

## Root Cause

- Mode: deduction from code plus checker trace.
- `TypeEnv::borrow` did not block non-strong mutable borrows. The MIR reborrow `_3 = &mut *(*_1).0` therefore produced a standalone `&mut Slot[...]` local with no blocked link back to `self.slot`.
- `check_call` then created a temporary local pointer for the callee `&strg` parameter, `assume_ensures` updated that temporary to the callee post-state, and `fold_local_ptrs` removed it after checking against the old bound. The updated state was dropped instead of being connected to the borrowed place.
- After adding mutable-borrow blocking, `PlacesTree::unblock` still only traversed `ptr` dereferences, so `unblock(*(*_1).0)` could not reach a block under an ordinary `&mut`; aggregate fold then saw `†{ Slot | * }` and ICEd. This confirmed the missing unblock traversal.

## Fix

- Mode: deduction.
- In `TypeEnv::borrow`, for non-strong mutable borrows, infer a weakened bound `t2` from the current pointee type using holes/kvars, check `t1 <: t2`, block the borrowed place with `t2`, and return `&mut t2`.
- In `PlacesTree::unblock`, traverse ordinary reference dereferences as well as `ptr` dereferences so the borrow-end ghost statement can remove blocks placed under `&mut`.

## After Fix Results

- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/reported.rs`: verified. Trajectory: convergent-to-fixed.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/direct_arg.rs`: verified. Trajectory: convergent-to-fixed.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/noop_setter.rs`: verified before and after. Trajectory: stable divergent control.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/no_field_invariant.rs`: verified. Trajectory: convergent-to-fixed.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/scalar_grow.rs`: verified. Trajectory: convergent-to-fixed.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/invalid_shrink.rs`: rejected with `error[E0999]: type invariant may not hold (when place is folded)`. Trajectory: soundness-confirming divergent.
- `/tmp/p08g-scratch/post_visible.rs`: invalid probe; parser/type surface rejected the signature with `expression not allowed in this position`, so not used as evidence.

## Regression Detour

- Mode: induction.
- First abstract-suite run after broad mutable-borrow blocking failed `pos/surface/loop_abstract_refinement.rs` with an internal incompatible-types error involving blocked `RVec` types.
- Deduction from trace: broad blocking applied to long-lived mutable borrows of generic opaque `RVec<T>`, keeping `vec` blocked across loop joins and perturbing existing abstract-refinement loop reasoning.
- Refinement: restrict inferred mutable-borrow blocking to opaque ADTs with no generic arguments. This preserves the `Slot` issue family while avoiding generic container internals such as `RVec<T>`.
- Targeted check: `tests/tests/pos/surface/loop_abstract_refinement.rs` verified after narrowing.
- Final regression: `cargo xtask test --suite basic abstract` passed: 7 UI tests passed, 5 compile-fail tests passed.

